{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אם חבול תחבול", :translit "im chavol tachbol", :gloss "if you take a pledge"} {:he "אלהים לא תקלל", :translit "elohim lo tekaleil", :gloss "Elohim you shall not curse"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parshiyot: verbal link between adjacent passages in the Torah text"}], :frame {:text "The hermeneutic of semikhut parshiyot reads laws placed next to each other as thematically interconnected (Shabbat 105b; Yevamot 4a). The verse forbidding cursbing of judges, 'Elohim you shall not curse' (Exodus 22:27), directly follows laws of pledge collection, suggesting the link: the court officer who seizes pledges must be warned not to curse the judge if the debtor resists.", :sources ["Shabbat 105b" "Yevamot 4a" "Exodus 22:27"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut parshiyot: verbal link between adjacent passages in the Torah text", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:34.101087231Z", :model "glm-5.2"}